  "description": "SINAMICS G120 inverter with CU240B-2 or CU240E-2 Control Unit (RS485, Modbus RTU): process data, I/O, converter data, diagnostics, faults and technology controller registers",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "Siemens, \"SINAMICS G120 Inverter with CU240B-2 and CU240E-2 Control Units Operating Instructions\", 01/2011, FW 4.4, A5E02299792B AB, section 6.2.3 Communication over Modbus RTU, table 6-30; https://pogoni.etf.bg.ac.rs/PLC_PLUS/Control_Units_CU240B-2_and_CU240E-2_en-US.pdf",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "SINAMICS G120 Inverter with CU240B-2 and CU240E-2 Control Units, Operating Instructions",
      "version": "A5E02299792B AB, FW 4.4",
      "date": "2011-01",
      "url": "https://pogoni.etf.bg.ac.rs/PLC_PLUS/Control_Units_CU240B-2_and_CU240E-2_en-US.pdf",
      "note": "section 6.2.3, Table 6-30 Assigning the Modbus register to the parameters of the Control Unit (copy of the Siemens manual hosted by a university; the Siemens support site refused automated download)"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Set p2030 = 2 (fieldbus protocol Modbus) with the macro P0015 = 21; the address comes from the DIP switches or p2021 (1 to 247, effective after a power cycle), the baud rate from p2020 (factory 19200 bit/s). The Control Unit is a Modbus RTU slave with even parity.",
    "Addresses are the manual's register numbers minus 40001 (40100 is address 99). Only function codes 3 (read) and 6 (write single register) are used; reading more than 125 registers or crossing the edge of a register block returns an exception.",
    "Valid holding registers run from 40001 to 40522. The manual says 40001-40065 are compatible with the Micromaster MM436 but does not list them, so only 40100 onward is mapped.",
    "The process data registers 40100, 40101, 40110 and 40111 are monitored by p2040 (factory 100 ms): the drive raises alarm F1910 (setpoint timeout) if they are not accessed within that time. The p2000 reference speed scales the setpoint and actual value words (0x4000 = 100 %).",
    "Written from the manual of the CU240B-2/CU240E-2 for firmware 4.4. The CU230P-2 and later firmware use the same Modbus RTU interface, but their manuals were not checked, so the map may differ from them.",
    "The manual lists no register with a fixed value, so the map has no reference values.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
